{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/939835-chi-using-mortals","id":939835,"title":"Chi Using Mortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T15:41:47-07:00","id":939835,"title":"Chi Using Mortals","content":"One of the types of minor supernatural creatures that did not get much attention were chi using mortals. You have Demon Hunter X and Shih, but they are both rare (maybe each group may have several thousand members), and I doubt they are the only chi using mortals in existence. What rules would you use for creating chi using mortals, let us call them mystics, who are not Demon Hunter X or Shih? What powers would you give them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T17:56:45-07:00","id":939878,"title":"","content":"DHX calls that out as Hedge Magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T17:59:14-07:00","id":939881,"title":"","content":"Use Sorcerer Revised and reflavor &quot;mana&quot; as &quot;chi.&quot; Done (OK, the book actually suggests this anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T20:55:22-07:00","id":939938,"title":"","content":"No, it is not considered Hedge Magic, and neither DHX or Shih have a separate background for Chi. They gain Yin Chi equal to their Self-Control and Yang Chi equal to Courage (similar to the Dhampyr of the Kuei-jin). I am just trying to figure out a reasonable cost for being able to access Chi and if it can be used for something else than martial arts and implants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T21:10:23-07:00","id":939941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/939835-chi-using-mortals?p=939938#post939938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it is not considered Hedge Magic, and neither DHX or Shih have a separate background for Chi. They gain Yin Chi equal to their Self-Control and Yang Chi equal to Courage (similar to the Dhampyr of the Kuei-jin). I am just trying to figure out a reasonable cost for being able to access Chi and if it can be used for something else than martial arts and implants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Chi is Quint/mana/etc what you point to is their natural Internal Chi reserves. All it does is mean you can hurt yourself spending it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T09:12:50-07:00","id":940104,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can hurt yourself spending it, but it is superior to the Chi of the Mana Background. It does one bashing health level per two points, soaked normally, if you used the Dhampyr rules that reflect the introduction of bashing damage to Revised. DHX and Shih can do a lot more with it than just modify difficulties of their rolls. They can power implants (if DHX) or Qiao (if Shih). I am just curious if anyone has any other thoughts about what Chi can do (beyond acting as Mana).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T10:23:57-07:00","id":940136,"title":"","content":"Make a Sorcerer flavored as Chi with the Flow of Ki and/or the Strength of Psyche Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:36:51-07:00","id":940162,"title":"","content":"You could, but their capabilities are not comparable to the implants of DHX or the Qiao of Shih. At best, they are sorcerers with an Asian flavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:47:36-07:00","id":940336,"title":"","content":"Well... I wouldn't be trying to recreate SF0 or the Shih, so I'm not really worried about that. Asian flavored Sorcerers = mortals using Chi for pretty much anything I could want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:08:58-07:00","id":940436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/939835-chi-using-mortals?p=940104#post940104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you can hurt yourself spending it, but it is superior to the Chi of the Mana Background. It does one bashing health level per two points, soaked normally, if you used the Dhampyr rules that reflect the introduction of bashing damage to Revised. DHX and Shih can do a lot more with it than just modify difficulties of their rolls. They can power implants (if DHX) or Qiao (if Shih). I am just curious if anyone has any other thoughts about what Chi can do (beyond acting as Mana).</div> </div> </div> </div>chi Mana and Quint are all the same thing. The fact that some can use it more impressively than others doesn't change the fact. If Hedge Magic and two KJ Disciplines(Which explcitly can be learned by Hedge mages) isn't strong enough.. um make Hedge Magic stronger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:46:51-07:00","id":940457,"title":"","content":"Well, Tzu Wei is a useless Discipline <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Wow, I get to give someone an extra die they can use under limited circumstances and it only costs me 50 bonus points to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:02:24-07:00","id":940464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/939835-chi-using-mortals?p=940457#post940457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Tzu Wei is a useless Discipline <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Wow, I get to give someone an extra die they can use under limited circumstances and it only costs me 50 bonus points to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>-1 penalty.. it could use more but still its a nice little effect since its the same damn thing over and over until elder.<br /> <br /> Really Hedge Magic covers most classic powers. You're going to be reinventing the wheel no matter what Might as well buff Hedge magic to bring it inline with the other Chi stuff than try to build something new its easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:40:10-07:00","id":940687,"title":"","content":"While WoD: Gypsies is a horrendously racist book in terms of narrative, I've always felt that the mechanics, if divested from the Roma ethnicity as a requirement, would make for a great kind of &quot;in-born magic&quot; motif. <br /> <br /> You can do that with Sorcerer, but there isnt much way to differentiate inborn magic from learned magic in that case.<br /> <br /> So you might look to WoD: Gypsy's Blood Affinities for inspiration on new Chi Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:29:26-07:00","id":940718,"title":"","content":"Yes, I have transformed the rules for Blood Purity and the Blood Affinities into something that could be used for a more generic minor supernatural creature that I labeled as Tennin (since practically every other name for supernatural creature has been used in World of Darkness). The Tennin would have difficulties associating with mortals caused by Blood Purity, would gained limited numbers of supernatural capabilities with Blood Purity, and would be able to learn the Blood Affinities. The Roma would just be one of the mortal races that had a disproportionate large number of Tennin due to their willingness to travel and to associate with the Night Folk (1% of their population would be Tennin, while the general public would have 0.1% of their population being Tennin). .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:36:42-07:00","id":945601,"title":"","content":"Qiao are essentially Hedge Magic Paths that the Shih invented, and chi-using implants are more-or-less Extraordinary Devices. Possibly ones produced by the equivalent of Enchantment. It's all Numina.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're playing mortals-with-Chi, you can probably just say that all the player characters can access Chi. There doesn't need to be an additional cost for that any more than there needs to be a cost for giving a character in a Mage chronicle the first dot of Arete or giving a Vampire the 13th generation for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}